  "count_definition": "Actual final executions across O0/O2 and P/E cores, not unique inputs. Native protected pairs compare represented GPRs/flags, system and segment state, active events and RAM. Return checks are subsets. The x64 counts use the rebuilt integrated NeverC; earlier focused and pre-integration runs are retained but not added.",
  "native_boundary": "Each compiled MOV is immediately followed by an explicit LFENCE. The oracle authenticates both opcodes, clones the pre-MOV register/system/event/RAM state and executes an independent encoding of that same two-instruction span. LFENCE ends MOV-SS inhibition before the debugger stop without changing represented GPRs/flags/RAM. Events within the shadow are not observed.",
  "negative_controls": "Each protected profile rejects a corrupted declared pointer or selector before an intact MOV. Used/unused reads survive O0/O2; ABI-compatible successes also check compiler returns and callee-saved registers.",
  "fault_observation": "Original #NP/#SS/#GP/#PF/#AC handlers expose their vector through completed OUT. Both restart PCs are authenticated before normalizing only that frame PC. Stale exception payload is excluded only after proving neither pending nor injected; all other event fields remain compared.",
